# What `vercel deploy` uploads. AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST.
#
# The Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore: without this file it would upload
# everything, `.env` with the secret key included. Listing what may go is the
# only form where forgetting a line fails safe — a missing entry breaks the
# build, it does not publish a secret.
#
# data/ and experiments/output/ ARE uploaded on purpose, although git ignores
# them: the API reads them, and the deploy runs from the machine where the
# pipeline wrote them (docs/DEPLOY.md, "Vercel").

/*
!backend
!src
!frontend
!data
!experiments
!track_record
!manual
!logs
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!requirements.txt
!vercel.json

# Inside what is allowed, what still stays home.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/.env*
backend/auth/migrations
track_record/*.bak
track_record/predictions_backfill.csv
track_record/report.html
data/processed/reports
# The experiments: only the M5 predictions the API serves, not the rest.
experiments/*
!experiments/output
experiments/output/*
!experiments/output/previsioni_m5_*.csv
# Logs: only the scheduler state /api/status reads.
logs/*
!logs/last_run.json
